A||||29||FieroLT1||Fiero LT1 make over pictures...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLT1||08-30-2001||01:05 AM||||Keywords: Maaco, paint, cowl induction scoop, badges.<P>This is the new look of FieroLT1 after a quick make over. This consisted of the removal of all factory badges, the addition of a factory wing, a functional cowl induction scoop from a 60's Camaro and a very cheap Maaco paint job. I did all the body work myself though.<P>The Before...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/before_640.jpg"> <BR>The After...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/after_640.jpg"> <P>And off course, her heart...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PA010007.JPG"> <P>The complete story of the make over can be found at <A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com/paintnews.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com/paintnews.htm</A> <P>Those attending this year's Fierorama will be able to appreciate her in person.<P>The main idea here was to build the ultimate sleeper. What do you think?<P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||08-30-2001||01:21 AM||||I could use one of those LT1 engine badges...where did you get it??<P>||||reg||14
Z||000002||MooCow||08-30-2001||01:28 AM||||Wow not bad at all.  I will be at Fieroramma so I can see it in person.  So if I see it can I ride in it??  Ive always wantd to ride in a V8 Fiero.  You can ride in mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-30-2001||03:09 AM||||DUDE! What did you do?! I cant believe that you took not only a Formula w/an LT1 engine in it, but also the fact that you spent all that time on the prep work, to MAACO?!! EEK! Why? Not only that, but they painted the trim on the wheels, now it looks like Night Rider. You had it all going on perfectly UNTIL you had MAACO perform their cheap work. Sorry, I dont mean to bash you or anything, but if it was strictly because of money, I would have rather kept it stock fading than to have a cheap Maaco paint job. Take my word, that paint job wont last long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>(Other than the paint, it is a sweet ass car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )||||reg||4
Z||000004||FieroLT1||08-30-2001||07:54 AM||||I know, I know. Heck, I knew that going in. I am very familiar with the type of work they do there. But it all came down to economics. You see, the best quote I got from a "very" reputable shop was $3000. That Maaco job was only $300. If you do the quick math, you'll soon figure out, much like I did, that assuming the paint lasts only a year (I am hopping for two), I can take it back "EVERY YEAR" for "TEN" years. To me, that's were the savings are.<BR>Besides, the guy shooting the paint at Maaco, was a buddy of mine and for the cheapest package price, once inside the booth, he spayed the best paint (two components). This is not the OEM Pontiac Black either, it is called Starfire High Gloss Black. On top of that, he added clear coat free of charge.<BR>Otherwise, I agree with you. All things being equal, I've took it somewhere else.<BR>The wheels trim? No, no, that was me. They are bad, but not that bad.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>  I like the look of the black trim. Alumium was scratched badly and it look ugly-er.<P>MooCow: I'll see you there!<P>LT1 ChopTop: I bought that Billet Aluminum Plate 5 years ago. Back then, I had to have it custom made because nobody made a raised lettering LT1. But nowadays there are a dime a dozen. Everyone sells them with different styles and colors too. Just search the web for them.<P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||08-30-2001||08:41 AM||||With that hood scoop and the sound of that LT1 it ain't no sleeper! Looks different. Just be careful at night. No one will see you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||08-30-2001||12:30 PM||||Nice paint job.  Hope it lasts.  If you did the prep and used their best paint (especially with a friend actually taking his time to do it right), you should be ok.  Those places save most of their money in quick jobs and cheap paint.  <P>Not sure how I feel about the painted air dam.  It looks better than original, but the shiny dam looks a bit weird.  I might have just put Armor all or something on it.  Or paint it with a semi-gloss or satin-black.  I'd also re-polish the wheel rims.  That or maybe put on some silver center caps and chrome lug nuts.  It's too much black - needs a little something to break up the lines.<P>Spoiler looks great.  Are you gonna put the Formula decal back on?  I would, IMO.  <P>Love your car, man.  Was the LT1 much harder to do than a regular TPI V8?  I'd love to put an LT1 in my Formula!<P>||||reg||6
Z||000007||artherd||08-30-2001||01:43 PM||||mmmm I like George's hood scoops better (much less intrusive though that might have been the look you are going for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cool car, needs a set of 17" wheels like I-don't-know-what, then will be complete!!<P>Sounds like you actually got decent paint out of Maaco, tell us how it lasts!<P>Hey, have you thought about making a 'matching' stock scoop on the passenger side of your car?  you could run cold-air to the engine that way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!!!<BR>Ben.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||Mach10||08-30-2001||04:23 PM||||It's different... Not sure... <BR>Ah hell. I likes it. Thumbs up!||||reg||14
Z||000009||HummelHund||08-30-2001||05:00 PM||||Isn't that one of the cars in Mad Max? That's the meanest looking coupe-bodied Fiero I've ever seen. The all black no chrome look really works out, I like the fully painted wheels. I'd say it might be a sleeper except for that giant cowl induction scoop on the hood. I think that gives away its sporting nature.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> If it were me, I'd put the Fiero badges back on, show some Fiero pride!<P><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>84' SE 2M4 WS6 (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
Z||000010||MikeSchaefer||08-30-2001||05:42 PM||||I personally love the look of your total-black car, it is very cool.  I think it is what will set your car apart from any others at shows (well that and the LT1  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<BR>Great work man,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||FormulaJoe||08-30-2001||08:22 PM||||Personally I like the total blackout look.  Reminds me of an AMG Hammer I saw once.  It was all black with dark tinted windows.  Only "color" was the three pointed star on the hood/radiator, very small and understated.    All in all a nice job.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroLT1||08-30-2001||11:12 PM||||You Guys!!!<BR>I was hopping you'd help me decide on the black wheels thing. You see, they are painted, but "digitaly".<BR>The car still looks like this...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trueone.jpg"> <BR>I wanted to see what kind reactions would I get. But instead it is an even split. Three people liked the black edge on the wheels, and three didn't care much for it.<BR>Now I don't know what to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>They are in pretty bad shape. The clear coat is peeling and they are badly dented and stained.<BR>Oh well, I'll think about it. Thank you all for your comments and input.<BR>Here is another picture for the road.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/frontone.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
