Z||000015||Standard||08-30-2001||11:39 PM||||Stay with the silver rims!  just my opinion, but I think they look horrible blacked out.<P>Otherwise it looks sweet!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||08-31-2001||12:26 AM||||You might be able to pull it off if you lower it, but I still like the silver edges. <BR>Maybe you can score a cheap set of rims at a swap meet or something.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Urchin||08-31-2001||12:36 AM||||Car looks great, but I would also say that the silver edges on the rims set it off better.  I also have to agree with Formula88 on the chin spoiler.  Needs to be a flatter black.  Spoiler and hood looks great, so what about that formula sticker? Is it going back on?  <BR>Looks slick though!<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000018||BlackDragon||08-31-2001||12:52 AM||||mako? where can i find this place? i couls use a cheap paint job. i understand it will not last long, but like she said, if it lasts a year, im happy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>im looking for a inexpensive black standard fastback. does not have to run. does not have to look good. only the mid section needs to be dent free. the fenders,bumpers, dont have to be in good cond. faded paint is fine. anyone who has info, email me. grey interior would be nice but beggars cant be choosers||||reg||1
Z||000019||My7Fieros||08-31-2001||02:59 AM||||Hmmm, yeah def stick w/ the silver trim on the wheels...you really need it to break up where the wheels and tires meet. <BR>Oh, btw, one thing you outta do....TINT THE WINDOWS!!! That would look sweet w/ the black car!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000020||FieroLT1||08-31-2001||08:36 AM||||Alright, I think I get the idea. I decided to  strip the clear coat off the wheels and give'em a good polish. I think it'll look good.<P>Formula88: I don't know. I've never don't a regular SBC before either. But, even with my limited mechanical experience (read none), this swap didn't seem bad at all.<P>artherd: I thought about it. But did not find one that I like. I am working on a cold air induction though system. It will feed from the bottom of the car.<BR>gt boy: Yeah, I have to find a way to turn that white smoke black.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Pontiaddict: I hear ya. A set of dropped spindles are on their way from Held Motorsporst as we speak. The rear has adjustable coil-overs alredy. So, it should be a snap.<BR>Urchin/Formula88: The "chin" or air dam was one the the things I specifically told them not to paint and they did anyways. I also told them not to paint the grills too, but guess what... THEY DID!<BR>I had already purchased the flexible plastic satin paint for the dam. Good thing is easy to take off. I will be repainting that soon.<BR>No decal or badges will be going back on.<P>BlackDragon: Maaco is a national chain. They are huge. Just look'em up in the book.<P>My7Fieros: Tint is also in the works!<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||10:00 AM||||I can't wait to see it at FieroRama... I remember seeing it at the Dells Run (if I recall correctly, it looked like a twin of antother black formula- Not anymore!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
