Z||000024||Raydar||08-31-2001||07:54 PM||||You could always strip the wheels and polish them. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Wheel.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Songman||08-31-2001||08:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>You could always strip the wheels and polish them. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's my vote! The black doesn't look right, but then with all of the other stuff blacked out, neither does the silver... <P>I'll tell you what would look good on that car! Either a set of black 16" Baretta GTZ wheels... like these but black<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.albertleaauto.com/AUTOS021.jpg"> <P>or a grey set of spokes from an 85-86 Chrysler Laser! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.allpar.com/model/daytona/daytw3.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000026||RossT||08-31-2001||09:27 PM||||LT, was your fiero the one at the Dells this yeat that wouldn't start?   Just curious as to what the problem was!!! Sure is nice looking!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000027||Archie||08-31-2001||09:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RossT:<BR><B>LT, was your fiero the one at the Dells this yeat that wouldn't start?   Just curious as to what the problem was!!! Sure is nice looking!!!!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, his was the other black LT1 Formula, the one that ran  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The one that wouldn't run was a car I built back in 1993. It has been thru 4 or 5 owners in the last few years. His problem was a bad distributer, he has it running fine now AFIK.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000028||RossT||08-31-2001||10:08 PM||||Thanks for the update!!||||reg||1
Z||000029||FieroLT1||09-01-2001||12:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>You could always strip the wheels and polish them. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm. Very Nice!<P>RossT: Like Archie said. That was my "twin" brother. I really felt bad not being able to help him out. I wish he had updated me on what ever happened to the car. He never contacted me back. (and I took him along for the Dell's cruise run)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
